#### 7. Sensitive Equality — `toStringFormat`

**Lines 84–88.** Asserts on the exact `toString()` format string. Any cosmetic change (e.g., renaming `items` to `size`) breaks this test.

```java
assertEquals("Catalog(items=1)", catalog.toString());
```

**Refactor → assert on the semantic property instead, or accept this as a deliberate contract test and document it:**

```java
@Test
void toStringContainsItemCount() {
    catalog.add("a", 1);
    assertTrue(catalog.toString().contains("1"));
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Trivial formatting changes cascade into test failures.

